Amongst all the useful items were some scrolls of identification
(which can be easily determined by its price). One of the scrolls
did a complete ID of my inventory. Really lucky, as I said. :-)

The stuff in the shop required that I had to stay on the first
couple of levels quite some time[*]. I had put all the stuff in
the bag - mainly because I feared that two wands in the shop (poly
and striking) could be picked up by monster - and finally my pet
picked up the whole bag - which surprised me, because I put in
all of the interesting stuff and it was quite heavy - and dropped
it outside the shop at my feet. But the amulet of reflection had
been one of the items that I bought in advance from my own money.
AFAIR[**]

Janis

[*] Partly I stayed on the upper levels due to an x-aligned altar
(really lucky as I said) where I sacrificed as mad because those
Tourist's darts vanish really fast typically, and I wanted some
good melee weapon; an important detail for Tourist survivability.
A long time I got nothing, then Giantslayer, finally Magicbane
(which was my hope to get - I love this weapon, especially for
those characters that can get Expert -, and I finally was lucky).
So another piece of my Tourist's luck was to have, besides BoH and
AoRefl, also MR. A really aweful lucky game.

[**] All that said as far as memory serves. I played a lot recently,
and I hope I haven't confused some of the facts from other games,
